horoughly tested. Here's a summary of what the regex does:\n\n## Regex Features:\n\n1. **IPv4 Address Validation**: Matches 0-255 range without leading zeros using `(?:25[0-5]|2[0-4][0-9]|1[0-9]{2}|[1-9]?[0-9])` for each octet\n\n2. **Date Format Matching**: Captures dates in YYYY-MM-DD format with proper month/day validation:\n   - January, March, May, July, August, October, December: 01-31 days\n   - April, June, September, November: 01-30 days  \n   - February: 01-29 days (as required, no leap year distinction)\n\n3. **Last Date Selection**: Uses negative lookahead `(?:(?![0-9]{4}-...)[^\\r\\n])*$` to ensure only the last date on a line is captured\n\n4. **Word Boundaries**: Enforces `(?<![a-zA-Z0-9])` before and `(?![a-zA-Z0-9])` after both IPv4 and dates to avoid false matches like:\n   - `user123.192.168.1.1` (alphanumeric prefix)\n   - `1234-56-78` (looks like date but isn't)\n   - `word2024-01-01word` (surrounded by alphanumerics)\n\n5. **MULTILINE Support**: Uses `^` and `$` anchors with `[^\\r\\n]` to work correctly with re.MULTILINE flag\n\nThe regex has been verified to correctly handle edge cases including leap day (Feb 29), boundary IP addresses (0.0.0.0 and 255.255.255.255), and multiple dates per line.","ttft_ms":189977,"type":"result","duration_ms":280818,"uuid":"77b87d69-6e72-48d6-bcdf-eb27f494de95","ttft_stream_ms":915,"time_to_request_ms":76,"queued_turn_count":0}
